parameters.text:
=Analyze these news stories from different outlets and identify bias patterns.

Topics: {{ $('Set Topics Config').item.json.topics }}

Left/Progressive Coverage:
{{ $('Fetch Left-Leaning Coverage').item.json.choices[0].message.content }}

Right/Conservative Coverage:
{{ $('Fetch Right-Leaning Coverage').item.json.choices[0].message.content }}

Neutral/Wire Coverage:
{{ $('Fetch Neutral/Wire Coverage').item.json.choices[0].message.content }}

Return JSON:
{
  "top_stories": [{"headline": "", "factual_core": "", "left_angle": "", "right_angle": "", "neutral_summary": ""}],
  "bias_patterns_detected": [{"outlet_type": "", "pattern": "", "example": ""}],
  "stories_only_covered_by_one_side": [],
  "framing_differences": [{"topic": "", "left_frame": "", "right_frame": ""}],
  "most_neutral_summary": "What actually happened today in 3-4 sentences, stripped of spin",
  "recommended_reading": []
}

=📰 *Daily News Brief — {{ $now.toFormat('MMM dd') }}*

*What actually happened today:*
{{ $json.most_neutral_summary }}

*Top Stories:*
{{ $json.top_stories.slice(0,3).map(s=>`• ${s.headline}`).join('\n') }}

*Bias Patterns Detected:* {{ $json.bias_patterns_detected.length }}
{{ $json.bias_patterns_detected.slice(0,2).map(b=>`• ${b.outlet_type}: ${b.pattern}`).join('\n') }}

Full analysis in Notion.
